  "problem": "$$\n(\\,\u2200x\\in N,\\,x>{n}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ \u2191 \\\\ \\text{I}\\end{aligned}}+1\\,)\u21d2(\\,\u2203z\\in R,\\,{{z}^{3}}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ \u2191 \\\\ \\text{II}\\end{aligned}}-1={y}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ \u2191 \\\\ \\text{III}\\end{aligned}}\\,)\n$$\n\nWhich occurrences of the variables in the expression above are free?",
  "worked_solution": "Let's examine our expression and mark the occurrences of the variables as bound $(\\text{b})$ or free $(\\text{f}).$\n\n- Occurrence I of the variable $n$ is *free* since it isn't placed right next to a quantifier and it doesn't lie within the scope of a quantifier that uses $n.$\n\n- Occurrence II of the variable $z$ is *bound* since it lies within the scope of the quantifier $\u2203z$ that uses $z:$ \n\n$$\n(\\,\u2200x\\in N,\\,x>n+1\\,)\u21d2(\\,\u2203z\\in R,\\,\\overset{\\text{scope of\u00a0}\u2203z}{\\overset{\u23de}{{z}^{3}-1={y}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ \u2191 \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}}}\\,)\n$$\n\n- Occurrence III of the variable $y$ is *free* since it isn't placed right next to a quantifier and it doesn't lie within the scope of a quantifier that uses $y.$\n\nThe occurrences of variables in the expression are as follows:\n\n$$\n(\\,\u2200{x}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ \u2191 \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}\\in N,\\,{x}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ \u2191 \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}>{n}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ \u2191 \\\\ \\text{f}\\end{aligned}}+1\\,)\u21d2(\\,\u2203{z}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ \u2191 \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}\\in R,\\,{{z}^{3}}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ \u2191 \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}-1={y}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ \u2191 \\\\ \\text{f}\\end{aligned}}\\,)\n$$\n\nTherefore, the free occurrence is \"I and III only.\"",
